# Caddy puts your DuckDNS address on the normal web ports (443 for https, 80 for the certificate check),
# gets and renews a free https certificate by itself, and passes visitors on to the bot, which stays private
# on this computer (127.0.0.1:8080). So the address has no port in it:  https://YOURNAME.duckdns.org
#
# 1. Replace YOURNAME below with your DuckDNS name.
# 2. Copy this file to a file called  Caddyfile  (no extension) in the bot folder.
# 3. Run:  caddy run --config Caddyfile
# See HOW-TO-USE.md, section 9, "Option C".

YOURNAME.duckdns.org {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}
